vkd3d: import upstream release 2.1, as Wine master has.

**The vkd3d inside our Wine is 1.18, and 1.18 cannot write an fx_2_0 pass that
sets state.** Wine's D3DX9 compiles effects through vkd3d-shader, and
`write_fx_2_pass` in 1.18 wrote every pass with zero assignments and stopped at

    hlsl_fixme(fx->ctx, &var->loc, "Write pass assignments.");

which is every pass a fixed-function effect has. Caribbean Legend's 54 `.fx`
files, compiled on the build host one vkd3d at a time on 2026-09-17:

    vkd3d 1.18 (this tree before this patch)   0 / 54
    vkd3d 2.1                                  8 / 54
    vkd3d 2.1 + 0076                          45 / 54

vkd3d 2.1's release notes: "The effects (FX) target can output numeric states
and shader objects in 'fx_2_0' profiles."

**This is Wine master's import, not a fresh one.** It is the libs/vkd3d change
of four upstream Wine commits between the 1.18 import (6b301ded2a9) and the 2.1
import, taken together:

    4c755ff7  vkd3d: Import upstream release 1.19.
    9a8e084a  vkd3d: Import upstream release 2.0.
    0a9c04e1  vkd3d: Remove unused files.
    9226b10c  vkd3d: Import upstream release 2.1.

with one line held back. 93deb5bb ("makefiles: Specify external modules in the
main makefile") renamed `EXTLIB` to `STATICLIB` in libs/vkd3d/Makefile.in as
part of a makedep change this tree does not have, so Makefile.in keeps
`EXTLIB` and takes only the import's own change, the removal of
libs/vkd3d-utils/reflection.c -- unused by any DLL in this tree, which is why
upstream removed it.

Microsoft's D3DX (the DirectX component) is still what games load first; this
is the fallback that a container without that component gets, and it is the
base the fx fixes after it build on.

